# Polyrepo "push" workflow

When the user says **push** (or "push all" / "workspace push") in this workspace, treat it as an explicit request to **review → quality-gate → commit → push** every dirty sibling repo. Do not ask for a second confirm to commit/push.

## Repos (each is its own git root)

`mfe-shared`, `mfe-backend`, `mfe-shell`, `mfe-landing`, `mfe-gateway`, `mfe-remote-admin`, `mfe-remote-product`, `mfe-remote-formengine`, `mfe-remote-vue`, and workspace root (`mfe-workspace` orchestrator only).

## Order

1. Scan **all** repos: `git status -sb` + `git diff` / `git diff --cached`.
2. Summarize dirty repos and intended commits (brief review to user).
3. Process **`mfe-shared` first** if it has package changes (publish before consumers).
4. Then other dirty product repos.
5. Bump + commit + push any consumers that need the new shared versions.
6. Workspace root last if dirty.

Skip clean repos. Stop on first failing quality gate or publish failure.

## Per-repo quality gates (run from that repo root)

Run every script that exists; skip missing ones. Prefer `pnpm`:

| Gate | Scripts |
|------|---------|
| Format | `pnpm format` then `pnpm format:check` |
| Lint | `pnpm lint` (or `pnpm exec eslint .` if lint script missing but eslint present) |
| Types | `pnpm typecheck` |
| Unit tests | `pnpm test` |
| Build | `pnpm build` — **required** for changed `mfe-shared/packages/*` before tag |

Do **not** run gateway Playwright e2e / backend e2e / Docker mesh unless the user asks. Do **not** use `--no-verify`. Scan staged diffs for secrets before commit.

Commits: conventional commits (`feat|fix|chore|refactor|docs|test|perf`), concise why-focused message. Push with `git push -u origin HEAD` if no upstream.

## mfe-shared publish (when packages changed)

Packages: `sdk`, `ui`, `interfaces`, `eform` → `@vuthanhthien99/{name}` on GitHub Packages.

1. Identify which `packages/*` actually changed.
2. Bump **semver in that package's `package.json`** (default **patch**; minor/major only if user said so or change is clearly breaking).
3. Quality-gate that package (`format`/`lint`/`typecheck`/`test`/`build`).
4. Commit + push `mfe-shared` `main`.
5. Tag + push tags (one tag per published package; tag must match version):
   - `sdk-vX.Y.Z`, `ui-vX.Y.Z`, `eform-vX.Y.Z`, `interfaces-vX.Y.Z`
6. **Release order:** publish **sdk before ui**. `interfaces` / `eform` independent.
7. Wait until publish succeeds (Actions on tag, or `npm view @vuthanhthien99/<pkg>@X.Y.Z --registry https://npm.pkg.github.com`). Do not bump consumers until the version is visible.

## Consumer bumps (after publish)

Update every repo that installs the published package to `^<newVersion>` via `pnpm add @vuthanhthien99/<pkg>@^X.Y.Z`, then quality-gate, commit (`chore(deps): bump @vuthanhthien99/<pkg> to ^X.Y.Z`), and push.

| Package | Consumers |
|---------|-----------|
| `@vuthanhthien99/sdk` | mfe-shell, mfe-landing, mfe-remote-admin, mfe-remote-product, mfe-remote-formengine, mfe-remote-vue |
| `@vuthanhthien99/ui` | mfe-shell, mfe-landing, mfe-remote-admin, mfe-remote-product |
| `@vuthanhthien99/interfaces` | mfe-backend, mfe-remote-admin, mfe-remote-product, mfe-remote-formengine, mfe-remote-vue |
| `@vuthanhthien99/eform` | mfe-remote-formengine |

Only bump consumers of packages that were actually published in this push.

## Report back

Per repo: dirty? → gates → commit hash → pushed? For shared: versions + tags + publish OK + which consumers bumped.
